# Backend guard wired into the suite: the shape tests prove the pass emits a
# carrier sequence, but only the backend decides whether that sequence becomes
# SIMD. This takes every operation at every width through
# `opt -passes=nybbler | llc -mtriple=x86_64 -mattr=+avx2` and fails if any
# kernel scalarizes, emits no vector code, or rebuilds a mask at runtime.
#
# See tools/codegen_check.py for why the kernels load from memory rather than
# taking <K x iN> arguments (the ABI unpacks narrow vectors at the boundary).
#
# REQUIRES: x86-registered-target
# RUN: %python "%codegen_check" --opt "%opt" --llc "%llc" --plugin "%nybbler" | %FileCheck "%s"
# CHECK: CODEGEN OK
